{"content":[{"c":["BEZER (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City of refuge in Reuben’s desert territory east of the Jordan River (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.43","r":"Deut.4.43","rawR":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.43","value":"Deut.4.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 4:43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.20.8","r":"Josh.20.8","rawR":"Josh.20.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.20.8","value":"Josh.20.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 20:8"},"), later allotted to the Merari family of Levites (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.36","r":"Josh.21.36","rawR":"Josh.21.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.36","value":"Josh.21.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:36"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.78","r":"1Chr.6.78","rawR":"1Chr.6.78","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.78","value":"1Chr.6.78"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:78"},"). It is probably a variant spelling of Bozrah in ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.48.24","r":"Jer.48.24","rawR":"Jer.48.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.48.24","value":"Jer.48.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jeremiah 48:24"},". According to the Moabite Stone, Bezer was among the cities rebuilt by King Mesha of Moab."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Bozrah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Bozrah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Bozrah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Bozrah #2"},"; ",{"href":"?item=CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cities of Refuge"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BezerPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 4:43","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.43","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.43","sourceRe